<BaseLayout title="About — Johary Ramaroson" description="Meet Johary Ramaroson, a Business and Computer Science student at Brandeis with experience in product design, debate, and student leadership.">
  <section class="page-hero wrap"><p class="eyebrow">A little context</p><h1>Behind<br />the <em>work</em><span class="accent">.</span></h1><p class="page-intro">I’m Johary Ramaroson. I study Business and Computer Science at Brandeis University, with experience in design, student representation, and debate.</p></section>
  <section class="narrative wrap section" aria-labelledby="story-heading"><p class="eyebrow">01 / My story</p><div><h2 id="story-heading">The path so far</h2><p>At Lycée Andohalo in Antananarivo, I spent three years as student council president, bringing students’ perspectives into staff meetings. Later, at United World College South East Asia in Singapore, I completed the International Baccalaureate while taking part in the Black Student Union and French debate team.</p><p>My education has also taken me to Germany for a PASCH youth course and to Dubai for an economics and finance course with the John Locke Institute. At Brandeis, I’m pursuing a BA in Business and Computer Science, with graduation expected in May 2030. I’m a Presidential Scholar, Business &amp; Economics Scholar, and Davis Scholar.</p></div></section>
  <section class="narrative wrap section" aria-labelledby="interests-heading"><p class="eyebrow">02 / What draws me in</p><div><h2 id="interests-heading">Room for curiosity</h2><ul class="interest-list"><li><h3>Design and technology</h3><p>At Cinch, I worked on wireframes, user research, and usability testing alongside developers. I use Figma for UX/UI design and have basic experience with Java and Python.</p></li><li><h3>Language and community</h3><p>I speak English, French, German, and Malagasy. Debate and student leadership have given me different ways to listen, communicate, and take part in a community.</p></li><li><h3>Beyond the work</h3><p>Music, swimming, and biking are part of my life outside study and work.</p></li></ul></div></section>
  <section class="narrative wrap section" aria-labelledby="now-heading"><p class="eyebrow">03 / A snapshot</p><div><h2 id="now-heading">Where I am now</h2><dl class="snapshot"><div><dt>Currently</dt><dd>Studying Business and Computer Science at Brandeis University in Massachusetts.</dd></div><div><dt>Previously</dt><dd>Completed the IB in Singapore, worked in product design at Cinch, and supported English testing for students with limited computer access in Madagascar.</dd></div><div><dt>Areas of focus</dt><dd>Business, computer science, UX/UI design, and communication.</dd></div></dl></div></section>
